            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is a favourite in our family for cold days and tradtionnal drunk on new years eve. \r\nOne advice: use a stick of cinnamon, instead of groud cinnamon: it's easy to remove and the smell and taste is better. \r\nInstead of what one of the reviews says: don't use wine that is too cheap or young. It urnes into 'vinegar' easily."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LBC"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for a party and it was a huge hit! I did add 1/4 c. cherry flavored brandy for each bottle of wine used, used cinnamon stick instead of ground cinnamon, and put everything in the crockpot to on low for about 45 min. until the sugar was completely dissolved, then switched to the keep warm setting and served it right from the crockpot. I quadrupled the recipe and ended up having to add more wine &amp; brandy, as everyone LOVED this! It was perfect for a chilly fall night.",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-04T12:54:49.553Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "chelmke"
            },
            "reviewBody": "With this recipe I use a broken cinnamon stick, dried orange rind, and whole cloves. I mix put them in a cheese cloth bag and let it sit and simmer with wine, cranberry juice, and apple cider.",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-18T15:43:44.300Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "alaska"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good as is, but I feel I made a few great additions. I added about 3/4 of a cup of water and used a cinnamon stick instead of the ground cinnamon. Also, the addition of 1/4 cup of brandy right before serving adds an additional kick! Very yummy!",
            "datePublished": "2009-12-14T17:35:38.410Z"
          },
          {
